<spell-notebook "form theming">
	<header level="1">
		Form
		<header>A form displays a set of related user input fields in a structured way.</>
	</>
	<form-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-form-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` included), or on the
			form's box through `::part(form)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias, so nothing inside blocks them; the form hands them to its fields and rows, so set them on the form
			(a field outside a form reads them from its own ancestors).
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-form {
			  --ui-form-gutter: 2em;
			  --ui-form-label-font-weight: normal;
			  --ui-form-required-color: var(--ui-primary);
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`inverted` swaps in `--ui-form-inverted-label-color`, and `loading` draws its spinner from the
				`--ui-form-loader-*` tokens. The `--_ui-fields-*` tokens are private (a row hands them to its fields): use
				`width` and `widths` instead. Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-form" playground>
				<ui-form>
					<ui-field label="First Name">
						<ui-input id="fm-types-first-playground" name="first-name" placeholder="First Name"></>
					</>
					<ui-field label="Last Name">
						<ui-input id="fm-types-last-playground" name="last-name" placeholder="Last Name"></>
					</>
					<ui-field>
						<ui-checkbox name="terms">I agree to the Terms and Conditions</>
					</>
					<ui-button type="submit">Submit</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
